From 1de956961ea5cff4b29ced16de5001ecc759ac82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John KNIPPER <code@jkn.me>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 03:59:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 693/696] build: generate AArch64 import trampolines for the
 shared engine libraries

v8.library and blink_platform.library are reached through generated
trampolines whose first call resolves the mangled symbol and caches it in a
writable slot. The generators emitted x86-64 assembly only. Add an AArch64
emitter, shared by both generators and selected by GN's current_cpu:

- each import loads its slot address with the large-model MOVZ/MOVK
  relocations (code and data hunks are placed independently) and branches
  through it;
- the slot starts at the import's slow entry, which puts the import index
  in x17 and enters the slow path;
- the slow path preserves x0-x7, the indirect-result register x8 and
  q0-q7, calls the resolver and tail-branches to the target through x16,
  so stack arguments and variadic calls pass unchanged.

The x64 output of both generators is byte-identical to before.

Tested: both manifests assemble for aarch64-unknown-aros (relocations
ABS64, MOVW_UABS_G0-G3, JUMP26, CALL26, all accepted by the AROS loader);
a probe that routes four imports through the emitted trampolines (ten
integer arguments, ten floating-point and integer arguments, a 32-byte
struct returned through x8, a variadic call), each called twice, passes on
AArch64 AROS in QEMU and resolves each import exactly once.
